      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not a doctor, but I can provide general guidance. If you have stage 3 kidney disease, it's crucial to consult with your healthcare provider before taking any supplement, especially potassium. Taking 99mg of potassium supplements regularly, especially on a frequent basis, may put a strain on your kidneys, which could worsen your condition. Your healthcare provider can assess your individual needs and recommend the most suitable course of action to manage your potassium levels and overall health.",
